\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Infinite God, to Thee we raise
\par Our hearts in solemn songs of praise;
\par By all Thy works on earth adored,
\par We worship Thee, the common Lord
\par The everlasting Father own,
\par And bow our souls before Thy throne.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Thee all the choir of angels sings,
\par The Lord of hosts, the King of kings;
\par Cherubs proclaim Thy praise aloud,
\par And seraphs shout the Triune God;
\par And: holy, holy, holy! cry,
\par Thy glory fills both earth and sky!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. God of the patriarchal race, 
\par The ancient seers record Thy praise,
\par The goodly apostolic band
\par  In highest joy and glory stand;
\par And all the saint and prophets join
\par To extol Thy majesty divine
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Head of the martyrs' noble host,
\par Of Thee they justly make their boast;
\par The Church, to earth's remotest bounds,
\par Her heavenly Founder's praise resounds;
\par And strives, with those around the throne, 
\par To hymn the mystic Three in One
\par 
\par \pard\tx720\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.Father of endless majesty,
\par \pard All might and love they render Thee;
\par Thy true and only Son adore,
\par The same in dignity and power;
\par And God the Holy Ghost declare,
\par The saints' eternal Comforter.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

